MetaML:
.sp 0.3i
.sz 17
.ce 2
A Meta-Language for
Meta-Programming
.sz 10
.sp 0.6i
.ce 2
A practical language guide and implementation companion
with DSLtk.hpp, worked programs, and language-building tools
.sp 0.8i
.pp
This book describes the MetaML implementation supplied with this repository.
It develops the functional, tacit, concatenative, and modular styles together,
then uses them to build language tools and embed an interpreter.
The final part explains the C++20 toolkit beneath those tools.
.pp
Read complete listings as independent programs unless their caption says
otherwise. MetaML listings use the standard library and the portable host
bundle supplied by the command-line executable. Pseudocode, descriptive
grammars, shell commands, and native-language fragments are labelled separately.
The companion checker runs each complete MetaML listing in a fresh process.
.pp
The book distinguishes implementation behavior from older design sketches.
In particular, ordinary evaluation is eager, strings are byte sequences,
module initialization is lazy, and the current C++ dependency requires C++20.
This repository's MetaML is an embeddable ML dialect; the name does not imply
the quotation and staging operators of other languages also called MetaML.
.lua
book.contents()
.endlua
